# Seamless Login with AES-256 Encrypted Payload

The goal is to seamlessly log users in via a URL, responding to a payload constructed by a PHP client (`?payload="..."`). We will modify the new **[DirectLogin](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-73) Action** to catch this single encrypted parameter. 

## Proposed Changes

### [LoginController.cs](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs)

#### [MODIFY] [LoginController.cs](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs)(file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs)

**1. Modify [DirectLogin](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-73) to catch `payload` parameter:** 
The method will now catch a single param `payload`, decrypt it to a query string (e.g., `UserID=PSCouncilAyurved&timestamp=1690000000&token=AuthorizationToken`), and parse out the individual variables.

```csharp
[HttpGet]
[AllowAnonymous]
public ActionResult DirectLogin(string payload)
{
    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(payload))
    {
        // 1. Decrypt the payload
        string decryptedPayload = DecryptPayload(payload.Replace(" ", "+"));
        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(decryptedPayload))
        {
            // 2. Parse the query string e.g., "UserID=...&timestamp=...&token=..."
            var parsedArgs = HttpUtility.ParseQueryString(decryptedPayload);
            string UserName = parsedArgs["UserID"];
            string Token = parsedArgs["token"];
            string timestamp = parsedArgs["timestamp"];

            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(UserName) && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Token) && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(timestamp))
            {
                if (IsValidPayload(Token, timestamp))
                {
                    // 3. Authenticate & Session Setup ...
                }
            }
        }
        return RedirectToAction("Home", "Login", new { Error = PortalEncryption.EncryptPassword("Invalid login payload.") });
    }
    return RedirectToAction("Home", "Login");
}
```

